# Sentinel Lite commissioning parameters (ArduCopter 4.6/4.7), SITL reference
# for the demo site (config/sentinel.example.json: geofence ceiling 25 m,
# inspection altitude 12 m).
#
# The Lite has no companion computer. Its second layer against the Hub flying
# the aircraft is the flight controller itself: it accepts commands only from
# the pilot's ground station (MAV_GCS_SYSID), so everything the Hub (system id
# 245) sends is ignored. Verified in SITL (tests/test_sentinel_drone_lite_sitl.py).
# Because the Hub's own telemetry and parameter requests are ignored as well:
#   - telemetry stream rates are set here, on the radio port;
#   - Sentinel reads parameters and the fence when the pilot's ground station
#     downloads them over the shared HM30 link.
#
# Load with:  SITL_PARAMS=config/drone/sentinel-lite-sitl.parm bash scripts/sitl/start_sitl.sh 3
# On a real aircraft the commissioning engineer loads the equivalent set from
# the ground station. Sentinel only READS and audits these values.
# Both 4.6 and 4.7 names are listed; the firmware ignores the one it does not know.

# Command lockout: only the pilot's ground station (id 255) may command.
MAV_GCS_SYSID 255
SYSID_MYGCS 255
MAV_OPTIONS 1
SYSID_ENFORCE 1
# Losing the pilot's ground-station link (the shared radio) returns home,
# also during a mission.
FS_GCS_ENABLE 1
FS_GCS_TIMEOUT 5
FS_OPTIONS 0
# Pilot radio loss (ExpressLRS)
FS_THR_ENABLE 1
# Navigation failure
FS_EKF_ACTION 1
# Battery: low -> RTL, critical -> land. SITL's battery is 3S (12.6 V full);
# the real Lite's 4S pack needs about 14.0 V low and 13.6 V critical.
BATT_MONITOR 4
BATT_FS_LOW_ACT 2
BATT_FS_CRT_ACT 1
BATT_LOW_VOLT 10.5
BATT_CRT_VOLT 10.0
# Also set remaining-capacity thresholds on the real Lite (found in SITL: with voltage
# thresholds only, the FC kept flying while its capacity count was nearly empty).
# For a 4S 5000 mAh pack: BATT_CAPACITY 5000, BATT_LOW_MAH 1500 (30 %), BATT_CRT_MAH 750 (15 %),
# matching Sentinel's return (30 %) and land (15 %) advisories. Left out here because the
# SITL tests change the declared capacity to inject battery faults.
# Fence: altitude + polygon (the polygon is loaded from Sentinel's exported plan)
FENCE_ENABLE 1
FENCE_TYPE 5
FENCE_ACTION 1
FENCE_ALT_MAX 25
FENCE_MARGIN 2
# Return home at 15 m: above the 12 m transit altitude, below the 25 m ceiling
RTL_ALT 1500
RTL_ALT_M 15
# Missions: 5 m/s, arm and take off in AUTO from the ground station's "start mission"
WPNAV_SPEED 500
WP_SPD 5
AUTO_OPTIONS 3
# Telemetry streams on the radio port (TELEM1 = SERIAL1; in SITL, tcp 5762).
# Careful with the numbering: 4.6 names the groups by serial port from 0
# (SR1_* = SERIAL1), while 4.7 numbers MAVLink ports from 1 (MAV1_* = SERIAL0,
# the USB port; MAV2_* = SERIAL1). Checked in SITL 4.7.2: MAV1_* rates produce
# nothing on SERIAL1, MAV2_* rates do.
MAV2_EXT_STAT 2
MAV2_POSITION 4
MAV2_EXTRA1 4
MAV2_EXTRA2 2
MAV2_EXTRA3 2
SR1_EXT_STAT 2
SR1_POSITION 4
SR1_EXTRA1 4
SR1_EXTRA2 2
SR1_EXTRA3 2
# On the real Lite also: MNT1_TYPE 8 (SIYI A8 mini gimbal on a serial port with
# SERIALn_PROTOCOL 8). SITL has no SIYI gimbal attached, so it is left out here and
# the audit reports it as a non-blocking finding.
